  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the mechanism decision. Part A (live verification) runs FIRST and its matrix (relationship × {new child, existing child, reparent, share, modify, unshare, MDA share}) is recorded before any code is written. The platform cascade is chosen for a case ONLY where the matrix shows it works; every case it does not cover is covered by the BFF synchronizer. A mix is allowed; a gap is not.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: never wider than the parent. For every child, principals with access ⊆ the root's POA share set, and each principal's rights on the child ≤ its rights on the root (same `RecordShareLevels` mask; ShareAccess and AssignAccess are never added on a child beyond what the principal holds on the root). A principal not shared on the root never gets a child share, including via a child that belongs to a DIFFERENT secure root.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: which children. Only children of a secure root are mirrored: children owned by task 144's named Secure owner team (per task 146), plus — inside a task-148 provisioning pass only — a child of the root being provisioned immediately before its re-own. Children of non-secure roots are never touched by the synchronizer (a platform cascade that would touch them is an escalation, not a silent side effect).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003 / owner C4 (added by review 2026-09-30)">Scope: deployment of the mechanism. If any case — in particular an OOB MDA UNSHARE of a secure root — is covered only by reconcile(root) rather than by the platform cascade, the removed user keeps child access until reconcile runs; with no scheduled run (task 148 builds the job, task 147 schedules it) that window is unbounded. In that case 146+149 MUST NOT reach a shared environment until reconcile(root) runs on a schedule (148 job + 147 schedule, or an interim schedule of the same job) OR the owner has accepted the window in writing. Removing OOB sharing of secure roots is NOT an available fix without owner sign-off: it contradicts the owner's C4 answer that users with write access can share OOB.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: other root-share writers. The fan-out and the "never wider" rule cover every BFF path that writes or removes a POA share on a secure root, including task 142's systemuser auto-share and task 143's No-Access enforcer; before any child-share write, task 143's guard is consulted if 143 has landed (else 143 wires it — `143-no-access-internal-secure-shares.poml:246`). Whichever of 142/143/149 lands second does the wiring and its test.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Scope: every share write. A share read that fails blocks the dependent write (use `GetPrincipalAccessOrThrowAsync`, never the fail-soft read). A partial fan-out failure on /share-user or /unshare-user is reported to the caller as a message naming how many children were and were not updated (never a bare 500, never a silent 200), and reconcile(root) repairs it on the next run. Unshare fan-out failures leave the ROOT unshare in place (removing access is never rolled back to restore access).</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §11">Scope: POA writes. All child share writes go through `IDataverseRecordShareService`; no second POA client (`PoaShareClientSingletonGuardTests` must stay green).</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner D-1 / ADR-002">Scope: all enforcement. No Dataverse plugin. A relationship cascade change is a SCHEMA change shipped in the solution (source-controlled, via the dataverse-create-schema / dataverse-deploy skills), not a plugin and not a hand edit in the maker portal.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the evaluator. Do not change AccessibleRecordSetService or the SPA/Teams child-inheritance term (task 055); contact access is unaffected by this task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">Scope: live verification. MANUAL gate, no Dataverse in CI. Use existing non-admin test users in their current BU; never propose relocating users. Probe records are deleted afterwards and the deletion recorded.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests. No `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no DI-registration or ctor null-check tests. Integration tests under `tests/integration/data-mutation/**` substitute `IDataverseRecordShareService` (the documented seam). Every "never wider" rule has a negative test.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: this task's PR. Placement decision citing bff-extensions.md; publish-size delta vs a fresh master build (short path, Compress-Archive, both sizes, file counts), ≤60 MB; CVE scan.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner round 2">Scope: deliverable. 100% of the share paths listed in the background (plus any found) are covered here; nothing deferred.</constraint>
  </constraints>

