  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Declare rigor FULL. Confirm 144/145/146 merged; read 146's owner hook.</step>
    <step order="1" mode="prescriptive">PART A — live, read-only first: read `EntityDefinitions(...)/OneToManyRelationships` with CascadeConfiguration for sprk_project, sprk_matter and sprk_workassignment; record every root→child relationship and its Share/Unshare/Assign/Reparent cascade.</step>
    <step order="2" mode="prescriptive">PART A — probes in dev with existing non-admin test users: secure root R owned by the named team; user A shared on R; create child C1 owned by the named team → can A read C1? Share R to user B → can B read existing C1? Create C2 after B's share → can B read C2? Modify B's rights on R → C1's rights? Unshare B → B loses C1/C2? Share R to user D in the MDA (not the BFF) → can D read C1? Unshare D in the MDA → does D lose C1? Share a user-owned child C3 to A, then assign C3 to the named team → does A keep C3 (shares survive Assign)? Repeat for a document linked only via `sprk_relatedproject`, and for a matter and a work assignment. Record the matrix; delete probes.</step>
    <step order="3">Decide per case (platform cascade vs synchronizer) and record the decision with the evidence in the task note.</step>
    <step order="4">If any cascade configuration is to change: author it as a solution schema change, deploy to dev, and re-run the step-2 matrix for the changed relationships.</step>
    <step order="5">For every case not covered by the platform: implement the synchronizer (create/reparent mirror, share/modify/unshare fan-out from every BFF share path, reconcile(root)) over `IDataverseRecordShareService`, and wire it into 146's hook, InternalShareEndpoints, provisioning Step 5.5 and unsecure.</step>
    <step order="6">Tests: mirror at create; fan-out on share/modify/unshare; reconcile repairs an MDA-made share and removes an extra child share; never-wider negatives; partial-failure message; share-read failure blocks the write.</step>
    <step order="7">Docs (guide + write-path I-2 row). Build, tests, ArchTests, publish size, CVE.</step>
    <step order="8" mode="prescriptive">MANUAL LIVE GATE after deploy (together with 146): re-run the step-2 matrix end to end through the product paths (/share-user, /unshare-user, provisioning, MDA share + reconcile) and record it.</step>
    <step order="9">Update TASK-INDEX.md (`✅ [done]`) and the POML status; write the task note.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>A root→child relationship already cascades ASSIGN (or a cascade change would): re-owning the root at provisioning/unsecure would re-own its children as a side effect, interacting with 144's migration and 148's transitions. Record the configuration and ask before changing anything.</trigger>
    <trigger>A child linked to TWO secure roots (e.g. `sprk_project` = P1, `sprk_relatedproject` = P2) whose share sets differ: union shows P1's child to P2-only sharees and intersection hides it from people legitimately shared on one of its parents. Owner decision (CLAUDE.md §6) with a recommendation; until decided implement INTERSECTION (fail closed) and record it.</trigger>
    <trigger>Part A shows the platform cascade covers some relationships but cannot cover `sprk_document`'s multiple root lookups: surface the mixed design (cascade + synchronizer) before implementing, because two mechanisms for one invariant must be justified (CLAUDE.md §11).</trigger>
    <trigger>Out-of-the-box MDA sharing of a secure root cannot be kept in sync by any mechanism inside the reconcile interval the owner accepts: present the window (an MDA UNSHARE is an over-share for its duration) and the alternatives as a §6 decision. NOTE: removing prvShare on secure roots from ordinary roles CONTRADICTS the owner's C4 answer (session27 note: users with write access "can share (OOB functionality)") — it may be presented only as a §6.5 path-B change to that decision, never applied on this task's authority. RECOMMENDATION: platform Share/Unshare cascade on the secure-relevant relationships if Part A proves it (removes the window entirely); otherwise the tightest reconcile interval the job can sustain, owner-accepted.</trigger>
    <trigger>Part A proposes enabling Share/Unshare (or Reparent) cascade on a root→child relationship: the configuration is table-wide, so every NON-secure project/matter/work assignment's children would also be shared whenever the root is shared (a widening relative to today, e.g. a share to a user outside the root's BU now reaches all its children). Present the change for non-secure roots to the owner before applying it; the owner's "same access as the main record" rule suggests it is desired, but it is a behaviour change across the whole product.</trigger>
    <trigger>Mirroring ShareAccess onto children (task 139 gives Collaborate/Full sharees ShareAccess on the root) lets a sharee OOB-share an individual CHILD to someone not shared on the root; reconcile(root) would then revoke that share, fighting a legitimate-looking user action. Owner decision (§6) with a RECOMMENDATION: omit ShareAccess from child mirrors (allowed — narrower than the root) so sharing happens at the root and fans out; until decided, implement the omission and record it.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>`IDataverseRecordShareService` (`Services/Access/IDataverseRecordShareService.cs:31-67`) is the only POA client; its callers share ROOTS only (grep `recordShare.(Grant|Modify|Revoke)AccessAsync` → `InternalShareEndpoints.cs:344,346,464`, `ProvisionProjectEndpoint.cs:726,754`, `UnsecureProjectEndpoint.cs:373`, `PlaybookSharingService.cs:321,336`). Nothing mirrors a root's shares onto its children (grep "child" in those files → no share call on a child row). No relationship cascade configuration is tracked in the repo.</existing>
    <extension>Prefer the platform cascade (no new code) wherever Part A proves it. A new `SecureChildShareSynchronizer` is added only for the cases the cascade does not cover; it cannot live inside `IDataverseRecordShareService` (a pass-through testing seam per its own remarks) or inside InternalShareEndpoints (the same logic is needed by 146's create hook, provisioning, unsecure and the 147/148 reconcile).</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>After task 146, every internal user shared on a secure project, matter or work assignment — including its creator — can no longer open any of its documents, events, to-dos or communications in MDA or Office; and shares made on a secure root in the MDA never reach its children.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

