  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The task note contains the Part A evidence matrix (every root→child relationship's cascade configuration + the probe results for new child, existing child, reparent, share, modify, unshare, MDA share, for project, matter and work assignment, including a `sprk_relatedproject`-only document) and the per-case mechanism decision.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given user A shared on secure root R, a child created under R after the share is readable by A with rights equal to A's rights on R.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given existing children of R, sharing R to user B (via /share-user or provisioning) makes every child readable by B at B's rights on R; modifying B's rights on R changes them on every child; unsharing B removes B from every child.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A share made on R in the MDA (outside the BFF) reaches every child, and an UNSHARE made on R in the MDA removes the user from every child — immediately via cascade, or at the next reconcile(R), per the recorded decision; if reconcile is the mechanism, the deployment-gating constraint's condition (scheduled reconcile or owner-accepted window) is recorded as met before 146+149 reach a shared environment.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The Part A matrix records whether a child's POA share survives an Assign (answer consumed by task 148's ordering) and, for any cascade change, its effect on non-secure roots with the owner's decision.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: a user on task 143's No Access List for R never receives a mirrored child share (guard consulted before the write, test), and removing a root share through 142's/143's paths removes the child shares — or, if those tasks have not landed, the note records which task wires it.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Child mirrors carry no ShareAccess unless the owner has decided otherwise (test asserts the mask).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: a user not shared on R never gains access to R's children; a user shared on R never gains access to the children of a different secure root R2; a child's rights for a principal never exceed that principal's rights on R (ShareAccess/AssignAccess never added); children of non-secure roots receive no mirrored share.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: when the root share read fails, no child share is written and the caller gets a message, not a bare 500; a partial fan-out failure returns a message naming updated/not-updated counts, and reconcile(R) completes it.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">reconcile(R) adds missing child shares, removes child shares whose principal is not shared on R, and narrows wider ones — each proven by a test.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AUTHORIZATION: /share-user and /unshare-user keep their existing delegation gate and rights narrowing; the fan-out runs only after the root write succeeded.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">MANUAL LIVE GATE (dev, deployed with 146): the step-2 matrix re-run through the product paths is recorded green with existing non-admin test users; probes deleted and the deletion recorded.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`PoaShareClientSingletonGuardTests` green; BFF unit/integration/ArchTests green; publish size reported per CLAUDE.md §10 and ≤60 MB; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: the mirror/fan-out/reconcile contract and the never-wider and failure negatives named above. Anything beyond needs a one-line justification in the task note.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Defect C10 half 2, session27 note C10 research gap 5; owner round 2 item 6. Pairs with 146 (ship-together). 148 calls reconcile(root) at provisioning, unsecure and backfill; 147 schedules it as the L4 safety net. Related: task 055 (SPA/Teams child inheritance — a different plane), 063 (share endpoints), 061 (creator share), 139 (ShareAccess on Collaborate/Full — makes MDA share/unshare of secure roots common), 142 (systemuser auto-share — another root-share writer), 143 (No Access List guard/enforcer — must gate child mirrors). Review 2026-09-30 added: MDA-unshare over-share window + deployment gate, table-wide cascade escalation, shares-survive-Assign probe, child-ShareAccess escalation.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load all files in knowledge before starting. Part A is read-only against metadata, then probe writes in dev only.</protocol>
    <outcome date="2026-10-02" branch="task/uac-r2-149" base="874bb1c2fe1058674fcdccbc496a3ca8559578f2 (task/uac-r2-146-b2-r2 + work/unified-access-control-r2)">
      <summary>Code complete, NOT deployed (ship-together with 146; G146-1 role 9 -&gt; 26 first). Part A read-only (spaarkedev1 2026-10-02): EVERY Spaarke root-&gt;child and child-&gt;child relationship has Share, Unshare, Reparent and Assign = NoCascade (only the system team / sharepointdocument / sharepointdocumentlocation relationships cascade), so the platform covers no case and the BFF synchronizer covers all (no mix). SecureChildShareSynchronizer keeps every Secure-team-owned child of the 23 codified child tables shared with exactly its secure root's internal sharees (users + teams; Read/Write/Append/AppendTo/Delete only, never Share/Assign; intersection over several secure roots), revoking every other share; never touches children of non-secure roots or rows owned by any other team; fails closed (root unreadable -&gt; no write; child shares unreadable -&gt; no write; undeterminable roots -&gt; held: only narrowed; grants re-checked against freshly read roots right before the write). Triggers: /share-user and /unshare-user fan out in the request after the confirmed root write (500 sdap.access.user_share.children_incomplete with counts; root write stands); secure provisioning Step 8; SecureChildShareReconciliationJob every 2 minutes (creates, re-files, client writes, MDA Share/Unshare). Full record: notes/task-149-secure-child-sharee-access.md.</summary>
