      <placement>BFF (bff-extensions.md: the fan-out writes in the same request as the root share; the reconcile is low-volume BFF-identity domain work on the in-process scheduler per ADR-052/ADR-036). NEW service SecureChildShareSynchronizer + 1 DI line (concrete singleton, ADR-010) — existing: IDataverseRecordShareService callers share ROOTS (InternalShareEndpoints, ProvisionProjectEndpoint, UnsecureProjectEndpoint), playbooks (PlaybookSharingService) and — CORRECTED in r1, the original text said "roots only" — two CHILD tables (DirectThreadAccessService: a user-owned Direct thread, and each message for its thread's participants, which r1 makes skip a Secure-team-owned message); no cascade exists; extension: not the pass-through seam, not the endpoint (provisioning + job need it), not the resolver (decides before the row exists); cost of doing nothing: after 146 every sharee of a secure record (creator included) loses all its children and MDA unshares never reach them. NEW job SecureChildShareReconciliationJob (AddScheduledJob) — existing jobs (external-access reconciliation, isolation census, membership) do not touch child POA; folding into the read-only census would give it a write path; cost: new/re-filed children and MDA Share/Unshare never reach children, deployment gate unmeetable. NEW method on the ONE POA seam (batched strict read) — one GET per child every 2 minutes would spend the app user's request budget; PoaShareClientSingletonGuardTests stays green. SecureChildLineage is a static map pinned by test to the codified role set and the resolver's child set. New reason code children_incomplete (the /revoke 500 precedent). No endpoint, package, option, column or schema change. Publish size: main session.</placement>
      <escalations>Trigger 1 (Assign cascade): does not fire. Trigger 2 (two secure roots): INTERSECTION implemented, owner decision pending (recommend keep). Trigger 3 (mixed design): does not fire. Trigger 4: MDA Share/Unshare and NEW/RE-FILED children reach the children within the reconcile's 2-minute cadence, not inline — owner decision 3 (accept the window, or a targeted inline mirror at the 2-3 interactive create paths, or the table-wide platform cascade); the deployment-gate condition (reconcile on a schedule) is met by the job shipped here. Trigger 5 (table-wide cascade): not applied, not proposed; guide lists it as must-NOT pending the owner. Trigger 6 (ShareAccess on children): omitted, owner decision pending (recommend keep omitted). Job ships enabled WITH writes (it is the mechanism) — owner may require report-only first, in which case 146+149 must not reach a shared environment until writes are on. Tasks 142/143 have not landed: per the constraint they wire the fan-out/guard when they land (they call SyncRootAsync; child sharees are a subset of root sharees by construction).</escalations>
