    <outcome date="2026-10-03" round="r2" branch="task/uac-r2-149-r2" base="1a72f97d1 (task/uac-r2-149-r1)">
      <summary>Second adversarial-verifier fix round; every finding dispositioned in notes/task-149-secure-child-sharee-access.md §12. NO production code changed. Five fail-closed guards that could be removed with every test green are now pinned by tests: V6 (the fresh root re-read failing: no grant and no widening written, revokes and narrowings still written, every such child not updated), V1 (a WIDENING racing a root narrowing or unshare is re-checked, not only a grant), V2/V3/V4 (a missing root, a missing intermediate parent and a chain deeper than MaxLineageDepth each make the child HELD; with no known root every share on it, a former sharee's included, is revoked), V5 (a table past the MaxPages ceiling fails the run and writes nothing), V11 (repeating a share after an incomplete fan-out completes it through the "unchanged" path, as the 500's "or you can try again" promises). The unsecure transition gap (owner round 7 item 5 "kept in sync on ... secure/unsecure"; step 5) is now an explicit SHIP GATE in guide §7a and owner decision 4 (recommended: no record is unsecured in a shared environment until task 148 is deployed), not only a deviation line. The 143 coordination is recorded as an orchestrator merge-order obligation (whichever of 143/149 merges second wires SecureShareNoAccessGuard before child grants and widenings, makes NoAccessShareEnforcer call SyncRootAsync, and adds the walled-user-never-on-a-child test). Decision 3 (2-minute window, writes-on posture, per-tick request budget) is restated for the owner.</summary>
